  "verbalization": "Naproxen is shown to have a target relationship with D-aspartate oxidase through two distinct pathways, with the first pathway linking Naproxen to Matrix metalloproteinase-28, which in turn is targeted by Capric acid, and Capric acid targeting D-aspartate oxidase. The second pathway connects Naproxen to Kallikrein 4, which is targeted by Decarine, and Decarine targeting D-aspartate oxidase. These pathways suggest that Naproxen may act through a series of intermediate targets to reach D-aspartate oxidase, potentially via different molecular mechanisms. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Naproxen and D-aspartate oxidase, though the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear. The presence of multiple indirect pathways indicates that the relationship may be complex, requiring further investigation to determine the precise mode of action and the role of the intermediate targets.",
